    "result_text": "The only test class is the acceptance test, and it passes. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI updated the create audit line in `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner` so it now also logs `membershipLevel` and `membershipNumber`, keeping the existing `id`, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate` fields.\n\n`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java:315`:\n```java\nif (isCreate) {\n    String membershipNumber = Owner.membershipNumber(owner.getCustomerCode(),\n        owner.getRegistrationDate());\n    int membershipLevel = Owner.membershipLevel(Owner.membershipPoints(\n        owner.getNamesakeCount(), owner.getEmail(), owner.getHouseholdCount(),\n        owner.getRegistrationDate()));\n    AUDIT.info(\"owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={} \"\n            + \"membershipLevel={} membershipNumber={}\",\n        owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate(),\n        membershipLevel, membershipNumber);\n}\n```\n\nThe values are derived the same way the `OwnerMapper` computes them for the API response (`Owner.membershipNumber(...)` and `Owner.membershipLevel(Owner.membershipPoints(...))`), so the audit line matches what the owner endpoint reports. The test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`), and the emitted log confirms the new fields, e.g. `owner created id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E registrationDate=2026-10-01 membershipLevel=2 membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M26`.",
