    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is clean, additive, and idiomatic for this codebase:\n\n- **Logic lives in the right unit.** The derivation formulas stay where they belong \u2014 the static `Owner.membershipNumber`, `Owner.membershipPoints`, and `Owner.membershipLevel` primitives on the `Owner` model. The service only *invokes* them to enrich the audit line; it does not re-implement any of the membership math.\n- **No duplication.** These are the same canonical helpers that `OwnerMapper` uses (`formatMembershipNumber`/`formatMembershipPoints`/`formatMembershipLevel` at `OwnerMapper.java:72-102`). The mapper's `format*` methods are private DTO-mapping helpers that take an `Owner`, so they aren't reachable (nor appropriate to reach into) from the service; composing the public static primitives inline is the natural path given the available API.\n- **Fits the surrounding method.** `saveOwner` already computes several derived values from the owner's fields (`generateCustomerCode`, `countNamesakes`, `countHouseholdMembers`) in the create branch, so computing two more derived values for the create-only audit line reads consistently with the existing style. The local variables (`membershipNumber`, `membershipLevel`) keep the log statement readable.\n- **Spec satisfied additively.** The pre-existing fields (`id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`) remain in the message; the two new fields are appended, and the format placeholders line up with the argument order.\n\nNo structural improvements needed.",
